    "result_text": "Claims now record who opened them, and that person can't settle them. All 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Database:** a new migration, `V10__claim_opened_by.sql`, adds an `opened_by` column to the `claim` table. It stays empty until the claim is opened.\n- **Server:** the claim class, its repository and the claim sent to the screen all carry the new field. In `ApplyClaimAction.java`, opening a claim saves the signed-in user. If that same user tries to settle it, the server refuses with a 409 and the message \"The user who opened a claim cannot settle it.\" The refusal happens before anything is saved or audited, so the status stays the same and nothing goes to the audit file.\n- **Screen:** each claim row in `Claims.tsx` shows \"Opened by\" with `data-testid=\"claim-opened-by\"`, which is blank until the claim is opened. A refused settle shows the server's message in the claim's existing error element.\n\n**Decision for you:** if an open claim is voided, it keeps its opened-by name, even though voiding clears the claim's number. The tests only void draft claims, so they don't cover this case. Clearing the name on void would be a one-line change.\n\nThe first test run failed because a Python setup from another project on the PATH stopped my edit script from running, so the code was never changed. I re-ran the same edits with the system Python, and that run is the one that passed.",
